@@ -35,6 +35,8 @@ UrlResolver is the main entry point for connecting to url:// protocol services:
 
 Low-level peer-to-peer networking, gossip, relay, and RPC stream functionality is provided by [UrlProtocol](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol) (`foundation.url:protocol`).
 
+The direct libp2p dependency includes [the published-connection settlement fix](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/jvm-libp2p/pull/73). Racing dials preserve a physical connection already selected by either endpoint, so later duplicate cleanup leaves accepted RPC work available.
+
 Gossip re-broadcast operations (forwarding service announcements, peer announcements, and service withdrawals to other peers) run in background coroutines to avoid blocking the listener thread. This ensures that slow network operations (e.g., connecting to NAT'd peers with 1-second timeouts) do not delay processing of subsequent gossip messages.
 
 Background peer-prune confirmations use separate blocking capacity, limited to one reachability check
